From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:03:44 +0000
Subject: MIPS: lantiq: unselect SWAP_IO_SPACE when LANTIQ is selected

The SWAP_IO_SPACE macro prevents the serial driver
drivers/tty/serial/lantiq.c from using readl/writel to replace
ltq_r32/ltq_w32, which are SoC/platform-specific APIs.

readl/writel are used in that serial driver to support multiple
platforms and architectures. The legacy Lantiq platform (Danube)
enables SWAP_IO_SPACE to support PCI due to hardware bugs: a
little-endian bus plus PCI TX/RX swap impacts both the data and
control paths. It is better to let the PCI device driver do the
endian swap, since SWAP_IO_SPACE is a global macro that also
impacts other peripherals such as USB. Other MIPS device drivers
are unaffected when SWAP_IO_SPACE is not selected because they use
the non-swapping __raw_readl/__raw_writel accessors.

This prepares sharing the serial driver with the Intel MIPS
(xRX500) platform, which runs big-endian with native-endian MMIO.

Originally submitted for the 2018 intel-mips platform series by
Songjun Wu <songjun.wu@linux.intel.com>:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20180803030237.3366-11-songjun.wu@linux.intel.com/

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/Kconfig b/arch/mips/Kconfig
index 83a6b68d8a39..a14646db07b3 100644
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -468,7 +468,6 @@ config LANTIQ
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_VPE_LOADER
 	select SYS_HAS_EARLY_PRINTK
 	select GPIOLIB
-	select SWAP_IO_SPACE
 	select BOOT_RAW
 	select HAVE_LEGACY_CLK
 	select USE_OF
